 "about": "Vectors for x402/exact/stellar/precondition (x402-exact-stellar-precondition.md): the 40-byte payload, the signed-payload signer, the build of the transaction the buyer signs, bound and reference, and every refusal of the profile. The fixed inputs are H = SHA-256(\"abc\") (FIPS 180-2), the seller from Ed25519 seed 04x32, the buyer from 05x32, a stranger from 09x32, the asset the contract strkey of 06x32, on testnet, and x402-exact-stellar.json's V2 simulated envelope (nonce 1) with its transfer set to transfer(buyer, seller, 10000000). The expected values were computed outside the workspace with stellar-sdk 13.0.0 (Python 3.12.3; its xdr, keypair, auth and signer_key modules): the payload as H then the nonce by int.to_bytes(8, 'big', signed=True); the signer as xdr.SignerKey SIGNER_KEY_TYPE_ED25519_SIGNED_PAYLOAD; the preimage as xdr.HashIDPreimage ENVELOPE_TYPE_SOROBAN_AUTHORIZATION; the transaction with xdr.PreconditionsV2 holding the time bounds the simulated envelope carried and that one signer, the entry signed by auth.authorize_entry and the payload by Keypair.sign_payload_decorated; command: python3 -I gen.py x402-exact-stellar.json <out>. Each envelope of refusedBound is that build with one member changed, written by the same tool; the option and choice rows of refusedFilter and refusedBuild change one member, and no tool writes their codes, which are the profile's.",
